{
 "author_name": "HeavyMap",
 "author_url": "https://heavymap.com/journey",
 "content": [
  {
   "children": [
    "working-paper, architecture, framework"
   ],
   "tag": "aside"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A working paper written on 2026-11-16, published nearly as written. Local file paths, private repository names and personal names have been removed."
   ],
   "tag": "blockquote"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Status:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " recommendation for review, 2026-09-30. Linear ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NIA-80"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", under Epic 2 ",
    {
     "children": [
      "NIA-24"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (gate G2). Docs and one synthetic fixture. Not a locked rewrite of the spine illustration."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "MCS:"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " no cells changed. No ",
    {
     "children": [
      "dataset_id"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This note says how a City of Rochester parcel gets the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "{local}"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " part of its HeavyMap key. It does not fetch parcels, sample owner names, edit the Master Control Spreadsheet, or publish a site. Publication waits on G6."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Recommendation"
   },
   "children": [
    "Recommendation"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Use the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "20-character section-block-lot as text"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (",
    {
     "children": [
      "SBL20"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). On the city layer that string is ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Copy it unchanged into the local token."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "ia:us:ny:rochester:parcel:{SBL20}"
   ],
   "tag": "pre"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Example of the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "shape"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", from the 2026-09-30 pilot (a real city id, cited as evidence, not loaded as a fixture row): city ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " ",
    {
     "children": [
      "04762000010220000000"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", padded print key ",
    {
     "children": [
      "047.62-1-22"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", Monroe ",
    {
     "children": [
      "countysbl"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " ",
    {
     "children": [
      "26140004762000010220000000"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". The fixture in this repo uses a different 20-digit string so the file is not that parcel."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The print key stays a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "display"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " native key. It is not ",
    {
     "children": [
      "{local}"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This copies the publisher’s digit string into ",
    {
     "children": [
      "{local}"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " on purpose. The same characters remain in ",
    {
     "children": [
      "native_keys"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " under the publisher’s field name (",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). That is a named minting rule. It is not a silent promotion, and it does not promote the print key."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "The Erie walkthrough in parcel-identity-spine.md still uses a print-key-shaped local (",
    {
     "children": [
      "SYN-999.00-1-1.1"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "). That illustration is not rewritten here. Rochester is the place the pilot showed the padding split."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Why-the-print-key-is-not-the-token"
   },
   "children": [
    "Why the print key is not the token"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Print-key padding is a property of the layer, not of the land."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "City of Rochester (",
        {
         "children": [
          "PARCELID"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        ", ",
        {
         "children": [
          "PRINTKEY"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        ")"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Print-key shape: padded, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "047.62-1-22"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Parcel id beside it: 20-character text"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Monroe ",
        {
         "children": [
          "Parcels_Public"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        " (",
        {
         "children": [
          "printkey"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        ")"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Print-key shape: padded, same city example · Parcel id beside it: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "countysbl"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", 26 characters"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "NYS Tax Parcels Public (",
        {
         "children": [
          "PRINT_KEY"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        ")"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Print-key shape: unpadded, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "47.18-1-33"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", and ",
      {
       "children": [
        "3.-1-1"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " · Parcel id beside it: ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " 20 characters; ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SWIS_SBL_ID"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " 26"
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Consequences:"
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "A string compare of print keys across layers fails when one side keeps the leading zero and the other drops it (",
      {
       "children": [
        "047.62-1-22"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " versus ",
      {
       "children": [
        "47.62-1-22"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ")."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Monroe ",
      {
       "children": [
        "printkey"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " is not unique county-wide: 267,357 distinct values in 267,962 rows (pilot, 2026-09-30)."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "City ",
      {
       "children": [
        "PARCELID"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " is the same 20-character shape as the statewide ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". The statewide layer has ",
      {
       "children": [
        "0 features for Monroe"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " and ",
      {
       "children": [
        "0 for Niagara County"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ". It cannot supply Rochester’s token. A ",
      {
       "children": [
        "CITYTOWN_NAME"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " of Rochester on that layer is a name collision (Ulster County in the pilot), so the name is not a join."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "The 1996 and 2012 Rochester assessment tables store ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " / ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL20"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " as a ",
      {
       "children": [
        "floating-point number"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      ". Digits are already gone (",
      {
       "children": [
        "4.62800001001e+18"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " in the pilot). Zero-padding does not repair them (0 matches in the pilot samples). Those vintages are ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_joined"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " by id. A float, an integer, or a scientific-notation string must not be cast into a token."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "SBL20"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " is text. Leading zeros are part of the token (",
    {
     "children": [
      "04762…"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " is not ",
    {
     "children": [
      "4762…"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ")."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "County-composite"
   },
   "children": [
    "County composite"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Compare New York parcels on ",
    {
     "children": [
      "6-digit prefix + SBL20"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (26 characters). Do not compare print keys across layers. Do not compare Monroe ",
    {
     "children": [
      "swis"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " to statewide ",
    {
     "children": [
      "SWIS"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ": Monroe’s field holds a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "municipality name"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " (or null); the state’s field holds a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "code"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "For the city, the pilot matched ",
    {
     "children": [
      "countysbl"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " = ",
    {
     "children": [
      "261400"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " + ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " on ",
    {
     "children": [
      "45/45"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " samples, with the same padded print key on every hit. Monroe has 64,655 rows with that prefix: 64,629 with ",
    {
     "children": [
      "swis"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " = ",
    {
     "children": [
      "City of Rochester"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", and 26 with null ",
    {
     "children": [
      "swis"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Unconfirmed."
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " Reading ",
    {
     "children": [
      "261400"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " as a SWIS code is ",
    {
     "children": [
      "inferred from the values"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    ", not from a Monroe code table. Keep the six digits as a native prefix. Do not stamp them as an official SWIS code until a code table says so. The same caveat is in the NIA-81 crosswalk (PR #54, not required for this note). That crosswalk marks ",
    {
     "children": [
      "261400"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " + ",
    {
     "children": [
      "City of Rochester"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " as ",
    {
     "children": [
      "inferred_from_prefix"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " and leaves the 26 null-name rows unresolved."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "A null ",
    {
     "children": [
      "swis"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " on a ",
    {
     "children": [
      "261400"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " county row does not mint a second municipality and does not, by itself, mint ",
    {
     "children": [
      "rochester"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". If the same 20 characters exist on the city layer, the city row is what mints the key and the county row joins to it. A ",
    {
     "children": [
      "261400"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " row with no city match stays ",
    {
     "children": [
      "not_joined"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    "."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Slug"
   },
   "children": [
    "Slug"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "rochester"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " is the recommended jurisdiction slug for ",
    {
     "children": [
      "city-published"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " parcel polygons. The spine slug is the publishing government of the grain. The City of Rochester publishes ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Monroe County is the geography-v1 county name and the publisher of ",
    {
     "children": [
      "countysbl"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ", which stays a native key."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "This does ",
    {
     "children": [
      "not"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " assign slugs to other Monroe municipalities. Their prefixes are a separate crosswalk, and the code meaning is still inferred. A single ",
    {
     "children": [
      "monroe"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " slug for every town would hide the city publisher. Whether those other municipalities wait, or use ",
    {
     "children": [
      "monroe"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " until a confirmed code table exists, is an open decision (Epic 2 decision 3). This note mints no ",
    {
     "children": [
      "ia:us:ny:monroe:…"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " key."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Native-keys-that-stay"
   },
   "children": [
    "Native keys that stay"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "PARCELID"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        " / ",
        {
         "children": [
          "SBL"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: 20-character digit text · Role: Source of ",
      {
       "children": [
        "{local}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". Also kept under its own field name."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "PRINTKEY"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        " / ",
        {
         "children": [
          "printkey"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: text, city/county padded form · Role: Display only."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Statewide ",
        {
         "children": [
          "PRINT_KEY"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: text, unpadded, when a row exists · Role: Not a join key. Monroe has no statewide row."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "countysbl"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: 26-character digit text · Role: County composite. Join key against ",
      {
       "children": [
        "prefix + SBL20"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "swis"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: municipality name, as published · Role: Not compared to a code."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        "Six-digit ",
        {
         "children": [
          "countysbl"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        },
        " prefix"
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: 6-character digit text · Role: Candidate code only. Meaning inferred."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "GISSBL"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: 10-character variant · Role: Not equal to ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL20"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". Not the token."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      {
       "children": [
        {
         "children": [
          "SBL_1"
         ],
         "tag": "code"
        }
       ],
       "tag": "strong"
      },
      " — Retained as: free text, sometimes several parcels · Role: Not the token. A later parse is a fuzzy join, not a mint."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ul"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "Housing-inventory ",
    {
     "children": [
      "SBL"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " matched city ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " on 14/15 pilot samples. Where that field is the same 20-character text, it is the same token, not a second one."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Duplicate-rows,-before-a-key-is-minted"
   },
   "children": [
    "Duplicate rows, before a key is minted"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "City ",
    {
     "children": [
      "TaxParcel2024"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ": 64,828 rows, 64,825 distinct ",
    {
     "children": [
      "PARCELID"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Monroe: 267,962 rows, 267,904 distinct ",
    {
     "children": [
      "countysbl"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    ". Fold the ",
    {
     "children": [
      "key"
     ],
     "tag": "strong"
    },
    " before minting. Do not fold by picking a polygon."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    {
     "children": [
      "Accept only a 20-character ASCII digit string. Leading zeros stay. A float, an int, a bool, null, an empty string, a scientific-notation string, or any other length or non-digit does not mint. The source row is ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_joined"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". Do not repair it."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Group city rows by that exact string. One group mints one key, ",
      {
       "children": [
        "ia:us:ny:rochester:parcel:{SBL20}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      "."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "Do not append a part suffix, an ",
      {
       "children": [
        "OBJECTID"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ", or a row index to ",
      {
       "children": [
        "{local}"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      ". A second key would change when the extract’s order changed."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "One row in the group: that polygon may be the outline."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "More than one row in the group: still one key. Do not choose a winning polygon. The outline is ",
      {
       "children": [
        "not_joined"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " until a later rule says the parts are one multipolygon or several units. The key exists either way."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    },
    {
     "children": [
      "County duplicates follow the same rule on the 26-character composite. A county composite mints a ",
      {
       "children": [
        "rochester"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " key only by joining to a city ",
      {
       "children": [
        "SBL20"
       ],
       "tag": "code"
      },
      " that already minted under the rules above."
     ],
     "tag": "li"
    }
   ],
   "tag": "ol"
  },
  {
   "children": [
    "NIA-79 (",
    {
     "children": [
      "industrial_atlas/ny_identifiers.py"
     ],
     "tag": "code"
    },
    " on PR #53) can report repeated ids and refuse a float. It does not choose a winner. This note is that policy. This change does not import that module. The duplicate-geometry question (condo or multi-part polygon versus two units) stays open."
   ],
   "tag": "p"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "Refusals-on-this-key"
   },
   "children": [
    "Refusals on this key"
   ],
   "tag": "h3"
